WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.859
In one minute, you will see how many people found your contest.

00:00:03.859 --> 00:00:04.940
We start on the map.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.230
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.471 --> 00:00:13.912
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:16.420
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.776
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:22.116
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.116 --> 00:00:22.799
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.836
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:29.960
See the three dots?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.466
Tap them.

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:35.114
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:36.927 --> 00:00:37.527
Tap Mine.

00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:39.388
These are the contests you run.

00:00:41.071 --> 00:00:43.121
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:44.508
This is your dashboard.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.306
Tap Promote.

00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:54.591
Activity shows page visits, visits from your QR code, and how many people voted.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:58.309
Below, a chart shows votes for each day.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:00.671
Use it to see which sharing worked best.

00:01:03.114 --> 00:01:06.144
Next up: Add sponsors and logos.
